{
  "title": "ramekin-core: cache the last uncompiled regexes and ~43 inline CSS \
selectors",
  "description": "Two perf/consistency warts in hot extraction/parsing paths:\n\
\n\
1. Uncompiled regexes recompiled on every call: \
src/ingredient_parser/item.rs:172,177,182 — normalize_digit_letter_spacing \
compiles three Regex::new(...) per invocation, and it runs once per ingredient \
line. src/extract/html_fallback.rs:333 (extract_ingredients_from_div) and :469 \
(html_to_paragraphs) compile a split regex per call. These are the only \
Regex::new outside LazyLock in the whole crate — move each into a static \
LazyLock<Regex> next to the existing ones.\n\
\n\
2. 43 inline Selector::parse(...).expect(...) calls recompiled per extraction, \
only 4 cached: spread across microdata.rs (11, e.g. :236,254), \
html_fallback.rs (12, e.g. :165,325), wprm.rs (9), extract/mod.rs (4, e.g. \
:427), blog.rs (4). Promote the static-string selectors to LazyLock<Selector> \
like the four already in images.rs/substack.rs. (The .expect()s themselves are \
safe — compile-time-constant selector strings.)\n\
\n\
Behavior-preserving, so no `make pipeline` data/ diffs are expected — but \
rerun it to confirm and commit anything intentional.",
